=== PE 899: Distribuition ===

Analysis of number-theoretic distributions:

1. Prime factor distributions:
   - ω(n) ~ log log n (Erdős–Kac theorem)
   - Ω(n) has similar mean but larger variance
   - Both follow approximately normal distributions

2. Squarefree density:
   - Proportion → 6/π² ≈ 0.607927

3. Divisor function d(n):
   - Average order: log n + 2γ - 1
   - Highly irregular, max ~ n^{O(1/log log n)}

4. Totient ratio n/φ(n):
   - Supremum grows like e^γ log log n

PE answer: 10784223938983273
